1
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,000
They broke every rule, loved every woman, took every risk and solved the most shocking murder
in the history of Beverly Hills. And it's all true. Give or take a lie or two.

2
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Sunset is a crime, mystery, thriller film directed by Blake Edwards.

3
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Tom Mix and Wyatt Earp team up to solve a murder at
the Academy Awards in 1929 Hollywood.

4
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Wyatt Earp, played by James Garner.

5
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Tom Mix, played by Bruce Willis.

6
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Alfie Alperin, played by Malcolm McDowell.

7
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:33,000
Cheryl King, played by Mariel Hemingway.

8
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Nancy Shoemaker, played by Kathleen Quinlan.

9
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:15,000
Victoria Alperin, played by Jennifer Edwards.

10
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Sunset is a 1988 American mystery western film written and directed by Blake Edwards and starring Bruce Willis as Western actor
Tom Mix, who teams up with lawman Wyatt Earp, portrayed for the second time in a theatrical film by James Garner.

11
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:57,000
Based on an unpublished novel by Rod Amateau, the plot has Earp
and Mix solve a murder in Hollywood in 1929.

12
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
Although Sunset has some comedic elements, it veers much more
to the period mystery genre of old Hollywood.

13
01:09:33,000 --> 01:09:39,000
Reviewers, such as Roger Ebert, struggled trying to define the film.

14
01:14:54,000 --> 01:15:00,000
Ebert noted: "The strangest thing about Sunset is
that it's not a comedy, not exactly.

15
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
It has some laughs, but it's a sort of low-key, elegiac mood film ..."
While Willis
received top billing in Sunset, Garner had more screen time in the film.

16
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
This was the second and final film in which Garner played Wyatt Earp, the
first being John Sturges's Hour of the Gun, released in 1967.

17
01:30:57,000 --> 01:31:03,000
This was director Edwards's second and final collaboration with
Willis, whom he directed in Blind Date (1987).

18
01:36:18,000 --> 01:36:24,000
The film explores themes of showdown, wyatt earp, murder, western hero.

19
01:41:39,000 --> 01:41:45,000
The tone is intense and mind_bending.
